# Build output
/dist/
/bin/sdlc
/bin/sdlc.exe

# `go build ./internal/tools/<name>` drops the executable in the working
# directory under that name. Ignored here, and the hygiene check refuses to
# track a compiled binary under any name, because this is easy to sweep into a
# commit with `git add -A` and hard to notice afterwards.
/linkcheck
/release

# Internal working documents. Never committed: this repository carries the
# product and what a user needs to understand it, and nothing else.
/plan/

# The loop's own story prose, when sdlc runs on itself. The machine state the
# gates need (tests.lock, gate-record.json, story.json) stays tracked; the
# model-written prose does not. This is a rule about THIS repository -- sdlc
# writes no opinion about what your project should commit.
/.sdlc/stories/*/ANALYSIS.md
/.sdlc/stories/*/PLAN.md
/.sdlc/stories/*/TEST-PLAN.md
/.sdlc/stories/*/THREATS.md
/.sdlc/stories/*/implementation-notes.md
/.sdlc/stories/*/retro.md
/.sdlc/stories/*/reviews/
/.sdlc/stories/*/diff.patch
/.sdlc/stories/*/diff.stat
/.sdlc/stories/*/logs/

# .sdlc/state holds one load-bearing file and two that are not: tests.lock is
# the freeze itself and belongs in history, while `active` is which story this
# machine happens to be on and cover.out is a build artefact.
/.sdlc/state/active
/.sdlc/state/cover.out

# Scratch paths the launcher and tests use
/.scratch/
*.tmp

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The binary the plugin launcher finds. Built by `task build-plugin`, never committed:
# the plugin ships from a release archive, not from the repository.
/plugin/bin/sdlc
/plugin/bin/sdlc.exe

# Built at release time, never committed: the checksums belong to a release
# that does not exist yet when the repository is at rest.
/npm/checksums.txt
/npm/LICENSE
/npm/*.tgz
